_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Make prefix fallback prefer the most specific model key.**

`get_pricing()` returns the first prefix match. With `gpt-4o` / `gpt-4.1` listed before their `-mini` / `-nano` variants, versioned IDs like `gpt-4o-mini-*` or `gpt-4.1-nano-*` will resolve to the full-model rate and overstate cost.

<details>
<summary>💡 Suggested fix in <code>get_pricing()</code></summary>

```diff
 public static function get_pricing( string $model_id ): ?array {
 	if ( isset( self::PRICING[ $model_id ] ) ) {
 		return self::PRICING[ $model_id ];
 	}

-	foreach ( self::PRICING as $key => $pricing ) {
+	$pricing_map = self::PRICING;
+	uksort(
+		$pricing_map,
+		static fn( string $a, string $b ): int => strlen( $b ) <=> strlen( $a )
+	);
+
+	foreach ( $pricing_map as $key => $pricing ) {
 		if ( str_starts_with( $model_id, $key ) ) {
 			return $pricing;
 		}
 	}
```
</details>

