_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Clean up the added filter to avoid cross-test state leakage.**

Line 119 adds a global filter, but it is never removed. That can affect subsequent tests in the same run.



<details>
<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-		add_filter(
+		$callback = static function ( $triggers ) use ( $custom_trigger ) {
+			$triggers[] = $custom_trigger;
+			return $triggers;
+		};
+
+		add_filter(
 			'gratis_ai_agent_event_triggers',
-			function ( $triggers ) use ( $custom_trigger ) {
-				$triggers[] = $custom_trigger;
-				return $triggers;
-			}
+			$callback
 		);

-		$triggers   = EventTriggerRegistry::get_all();
-		$hook_names = array_column( $triggers, 'hook_name' );
-
-		$this->assertContains( 'my_custom_hook', $hook_names );
+		try {
+			$triggers   = EventTriggerRegistry::get_all();
+			$hook_names = array_column( $triggers, 'hook_name' );
+			$this->assertContains( 'my_custom_hook', $hook_names );
+		} finally {
+			remove_filter( 'gratis_ai_agent_event_triggers', $callback );
+		}
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@tests/GratisAiAgent/Automations/EventTriggerRegistryTest.php` around lines
119 - 131, The test adds a global filter with add_filter but never removes it,
risking cross-test leakage; update the test to store the anonymous callback in a
variable (e.g. $callback) and use that variable in
add_filter('gratis_ai_agent_event_triggers', $callback) and then call
remove_filter('gratis_ai_agent_event_triggers', $callback) after asserting
EventTriggerRegistry::get_all() so the global filter is cleaned up; reference
the add_filter usage and EventTriggerRegistry::get_all to locate where to add
the remove_filter call.
```

</details>

