_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**`flex-wrap: wrap` conflicts with the single-row header objective.**

With wrapping enabled (header and provider selector), controls can spill to a second line despite `min-height: 40px`. If single-row is required, use `nowrap` here and handle tight widths in a breakpoint rule.


<details>
<summary>Proposed CSS adjustment</summary>

```diff
 .gratis-ai-agent-header {
 	padding: 6px 12px;
 	border-bottom: 1px solid `#dcdcde`;
 	background: `#fff`;
 	display: flex;
 	align-items: center;
 	gap: 8px;
-	flex-wrap: wrap;
+	flex-wrap: nowrap;
 	min-height: 40px;
 }

 .gratis-ai-agent-provider-selector {
 	display: flex;
 	align-items: center;
 	gap: 8px;
-	flex-wrap: wrap;
+	flex-wrap: nowrap;
 	flex: 1;
+	min-width: 0;
 }
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
.gratis-ai-agent-header {
	padding: 6px 12px;
	border-bottom: 1px solid `#dcdcde`;
	background: `#fff`;
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 8px;
	flex-wrap: nowrap;
	min-height: 40px;
}

.gratis-ai-agent-provider-selector {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 8px;
	flex-wrap: nowrap;
	flex: 1;
	min-width: 0;
}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@src/admin-page/style.css` around lines 407 - 424, The header currently uses
flex-wrap: wrap on both .gratis-ai-agent-header and
.gratis-ai-agent-provider-selector which allows controls to flow to a second
line; change both to flex-wrap: nowrap to enforce a single-row header and update
layout to handle tight widths via responsive rules (add a media query/breakpoint
to reduce padding, hide or collapse less-important controls, or switch provider
selector to an overflow/dropdown at small widths) so the header stays
single-line while remaining usable on narrow viewports.
```

