_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Guard callback execution so progress reporting cannot crash the loop.**

`fire_progress()` executes an arbitrary callable without protection. If that callback throws, the agent loop can abort mid-run and leave jobs in a bad state.


<details>
<summary>Suggested hardening</summary>

```diff
 private function fire_progress(): void {
-	if ( null !== $this->progress_callback ) {
-		call_user_func( $this->progress_callback, $this->tool_call_log );
-	}
+	if ( null === $this->progress_callback ) {
+		return;
+	}
+
+	try {
+		call_user_func( $this->progress_callback, $this->tool_call_log );
+	} catch ( \Throwable $e ) {
+		// Progress reporting is best-effort and must not interrupt the agent loop.
+	}
 }
```
