_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Critical: interrupts are persisted but never consumed — feature is a no-op end-to-end.**

`handle_interrupt()` appends to `$job['interrupts']`, but `handle_process()` (the background worker that actually runs `AgentLoop`) never passes an `interrupt_checker` callback into `$options`. `AgentLoop::check_and_inject_interrupts()` short-circuits when `$this->interrupt_checker === null`, so queued interrupts accumulate in the transient, are never injected into conversation history, and eventually expire with the job.

In `handle_process()`, alongside the existing `progress_callback`, wire a checker that atomically reads/advances an interrupt cursor on the transient. Sketch:

```php
$interrupt_job_id = $job_id;
$options['interrupt_checker'] = static function () use ( $interrupt_job_id ) {
    $current = get_transient( RestController::JOB_PREFIX . $interrupt_job_id );
    if ( ! is_array( $current ) ) {
        return null;
    }
    $interrupts = is_array( $current['interrupts'] ?? null ) ? $current['interrupts'] : array();
    $cursor     = (int) ( $current['interrupts_consumed'] ?? 0 );
    if ( $cursor >= count( $interrupts ) ) {
        return null;
    }
    $next                          = $interrupts[ $cursor ];
    $current['interrupts_consumed'] = $cursor + 1;
    set_transient( RestController::JOB_PREFIX . $interrupt_job_id, $current, RestController::JOB_TTL + 60 );
    return is_array( $next ) ? $next : null;
};
```

Without this (or equivalent), the new endpoint and `AgentLoop` plumbing don't connect.

