In `@includes/REST/SessionController.php` around lines 1062 - 1099,
handle_interrupt appends interrupts to the job transient but handle_process
never wires an interrupt checker into AgentLoop, so queued interrupts are never
consumed; in handle_process (near where $options['progress_callback'] is set)
add $options['interrupt_checker'] as a closure that uses
get_transient(RestController::JOB_PREFIX . $job_id) to read the job atomically,
reads the interrupts array and an integer interrupts_consumed cursor (default
0), returns the next interrupt (or null if none), increments and persists
interrupts_consumed via set_transient (extending TTL, e.g.
RestController::JOB_TTL + 60), and ensures it only returns array|null so
AgentLoop::check_and_inject_interrupts can consume queued interrupts.
